    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Kyle Tucker** (81.06) serving as our undisputed pillars of the lineup. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a high-upside matchup against Roki Sasaki; between the favorable wind conditions and Sasaki\u2019s slow delivery, the path for **Gunnar Henderson** to capitalize on stolen base opportunities\u2014our scarcest category\u2014is wide open. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** draws a highly favorable assignment against Trey Gibson (5.63 xERA). Both **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** (75.64) are positioned to exploit the weak opposing pitching and wind-aided environment, making them the primary drivers for our run and RBI production today.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved **Coby Mayo** (55.69), who narrowly missed the cut behind **Jacob Wilson** (58.23). While **Coby Mayo** shares the same environment as **Gunnar Henderson**, his dynamic platoon metrics against Roki Sasaki were slightly too suppressed to justify a start over the more consistent floor provided by **Jacob Wilson**. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Drake Baldwin** (46.69) and **Wade Meckler** (44.15). **Drake Baldwin** faces an elite arm in Jacob Misiorowski, and **Wade Meckler** draws a tough platoon disadvantage against Jeffrey Springs. Both reside near our benching threshold, and we will be monitoring their official batting order closely; should **Wade Meckler** be dropped further down the lineup, we may reconsider his status to conserve game caps. **Jackson Merrill** (52.34) also bears watching; despite a strong score, facing an elite hold pitcher like Jacob deGrom carries inherent volatility that could dampen his steal potential.",
